==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɪpɪŋ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shipping.wav|a=Southern England}}
*** {{IPA|en|/ˈʃɪpiŋ/|a=Upper Midwestern US,Pacific Northwest,CA,pre-/ŋ/-tensing}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪpɪŋ|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|ship|ping}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|enm|schipping}}, {{m|enm|schyppynge}}, from {{m|enm|schippen}}, {{m|enm|schipen||to take ship, navigate}}, from {{der|en|ang|scipian||to take ship; put in order, equip, man a ship}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|ship|ing}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|transportation of goods}} The [[transportation]] of [[goods]].
#: {{cot|en|carriage|haulage}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=52| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/21579039-chinas-growing-empire-ports-abroad-mainly-about-trade-not-aggression-new-masters The new masters and commanders]| passage=From the ground, Colombo’s port does not look like much.{{...}}&nbsp; But viewed from high up in one of the growing number of skyscrapers in Sri Lanka’s capital, it is clear that something extraordinary is happening: China is creating a '''shipping''' hub just 200 miles from India’s southern tip.}}
# {{senseid|en|fleet}} The body of [[ship]]s belonging to one [[nation]], [[port]] or [[industry]]; ships collectively.
#: {{cot|en|fleet|navy}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1606|author=w:William Shakespeare|title=w:Antony and Cleopatra|section=Act III, Scene 7|url=https://www.opensourceshakespeare.org/views/plays/play_view.php?WorkID=antonycleo&Scope=entire&pleasewait=1&msg=pl
|passage=Our overplus of '''shipping''' will we burn; / And, with the rest full-mann’d, from the head of {{w|Actium}} / Beat the approaching Caesar.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1724|author=w:Daniel Defoe|title=w:A General History of the Pyrates|location=London|publisher=T. Warner, Introduction|page=23|url=https://archive.org/details/generalhistoryof00defo/page/23/mode/1up?q=shipping
|passage={{...}} the Advantage appeared greatly on their Side, in Numbers of '''Shipping''', and of Men;}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1855|author=w:Frederick Douglass|title=w:My Bondage and My Freedom|location=New York|publisher=Miller, Orton & Mulligan|chapter=22|page=345|url=https://archive.org/details/mybondagemyfreed00doug2/page/345/mode/1up?q=shipping
|passage=My first afternoon, on reaching New Bedford, was spent in visiting the wharves and viewing the '''shipping'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=w:Robertson Davies|title=w:Fifth Business|url=https://archive.org/details/fifthbusinessnov0000davi/page/107/mode/1up?q=shipping|chapter=2|page=107|publisher=Macmillan|location=Toronto
|passage={{...}} I clearly remember a castle on the shores of the lagoon, where gondolas appeared amid larger '''shipping''', which seemed to be plying in and out of Naples {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|passage or transport on a ship}} [[Passage]] or [[transport]] on a ship.
#: {{cot|en|voyage}}
# {{senseid|en|cost of sending}} The cost of sending an item or package using postal or carrier services.
#: {{cot|en|postage}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''shipping''' is included in the quoted price.}}
# {{senseid|en|navigation}} Navigation.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|V|i|passage=God send 'em good '''shipping'''.}}

